    "done_when": "Read section 10 of a-finished-worktree-releases-without-a-force first. In reckon/cli.py, crew gc gains --pin-unique-commits, passed through to garbage_collect's pin_unique_commits option, and its help text names what the flag does and that it needs --apply to act. Touch only the crew_gc command. tests/test_gc_pin_flag.py drives crew gc --pin-unique-commits --apply through the CLI over one dirty, unintegrated worktree in a temporary repository, then asserts the archive ref resolves, the worktree is gone, and without the flag the worktree stays. tests/test_crew_gc.py, tests/test_gc_pins_unique_commits_before_release.py, tests/test_crew_help_names_its_state.py and tests/test_skill_contracts.py keep their base results. Record the outcome in docs/evidence/fragments/a-finished-worktree-releases-without-a-force/gc-pin-flag.html. Run `date -u` first and treat that instant as your start; your deadline is 60 minutes later. Write your manifest before starting any long command. Run both gate arms with pytest-xdist (-n 8 --timeout=300), never serially. Run the base arm, from a `git archive` extraction of your base under /tmp in a directory named for this run, and then the head arm, each in the foreground: a background command dies when your turn ends. Keep the gate to the test files that reach your change, tens of files rather than hundreds. Each arm uses its own basetemp outside any repository and writes to its own new log path, which it never overwrites. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder. Each log names its revision on the first line as revision= followed by the full sha, and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
